From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] setup.cfg: ship the bundled UnRAR license text

Upstream-Status: To upstream [upstream inactive since 2021, no maintained branch to submit against]

setup.py's license= kwarg only sets the Apache-2.0 metadata string for
the cffi wrapper code; it does not make setuptools pick up
unrarsrc/license.txt, the freeware license covering the bundled UnRAR
C++ source (unrarsrc/, fetched at build time from rarlab.com per
build.sh's init()). That license's own paragraph 2 requires its full
text to be included when redistributing software built on this source,
so declare it (alongside the top-level Apache-2.0 LICENSE, which
setuptools already auto-detects) via license_files, which lands both
under <wheel>.dist-info/licenses/ in the built wheel.

diff --git a/setup.cfg b/setup.cfg
index 9af7e6f..6db0d60 100644
--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -1,2 +1,7 @@
 [aliases]
-test=pytest
\ No newline at end of file
+test=pytest
+
+[metadata]
+license_files =
+    LICENSE
+    unrarsrc/license.txt
--
2.43.0
